    {
      "id": "de2844d9-cd90-457a-82d7-74288a908b24",
      "name": "Sticky Note2",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -1056,
        -1520
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 6,
        "width": 1728,
        "height": 1184,
        "content": "# How to configure this workflow?\n## Step 0: Configure departmentId\n- Open **Normalize Input** node\n- Enter the department ID you want the new tickets to be created at\n## Step 1: Configuring Zoho Credentials\n- Visit [Zoho API Console](https://api-console.zoho.com/#web)\n- Click \"Server-based Application\" and fill the form:\n```\n- Client Name: n8n_telegram_desk_sync (or whatever name you want)\n- Homepage URL: https://<your n8n domain>/rest/oauth2-credential/callback\n    (example: https://kaizen.com/rest/oauth2-credential/callback)\n- Authorized Redirect URIs: https://<your n8n domain>/rest/oauth2-credential/callback\n```\n- Click \"CREATE\"\n- Copy Client ID and Client Secret\n- Open any http node -> click \"OAuth2 API\" picklist -> \"+ Create new credentials\"\n- Fill it:\n```\n- Grant Type: Authorization Code\n- Authorization URL: https://accounts.zoho.com/oauth/v2/auth\n  (Top-level domain may be different. Use your DC (.eu, etc)\n- Access Token URL: https://accounts.zoho.com/oauth/v2/token\n  (Top-level domain may be different. Use your DC (.eu, etc)\n- Client ID: <Your copied Client ID>\n- Client Secret: <Your copied Client Secret>\n- Scope: Desk.contacts.CREATE,Desk.contacts.READ,Desk.contacts.UPDATE,Desk.tickets.CREATE,Desk.tickets.READ,Desk.tickets.UPDATE,Desk.webhooks.CREATE,Desk.webhooks.READ,Desk.webhooks.UPDATE\n- Auth URI Query Parameters: access_type=offline\n  (It's IMPORTANT to fill it, as placeholder does not mean default value!)\n- Authentication: Header\n```\n- Authenticate the Credentials and grant access on the opened window.\n## Step 2: Telegram bot setup\n- Open @BotFather\n- Open this bot's app (via clicking the button \"Open\")\n- Click **Create new bot**\n- Enter required data\n- Copy bot API access token\n- Use it to create a new credential at **Telegram Trigger** and **Send Agent Reply to Telegram** nodes\n\n## Step 3: Publish this workflow\n- Check all HTTP nodes and verify their Top-Level Domain (.com) is the same as your Zoho Desk's (i.e. you may need to change it to .eu)\n- Click on **Publish** button at the top right\n\n## Step 4: Database and Webhook\n**NOTE: IT'S VERY IMPORTANT THAT YOU FINISH ALL PREVIOUS STEPS AND PUBLISH THE WORKFLOW FIRST\n(because webhook registration requires published webhook endpoint that Zoho can verify)**\n- Press **Execute Workflow** when hovering near the **Initial Setup** trigger node.\n\n## Step 5: (OPTIONAL) Disable Zoho Desk default notification of public comment\nBy default - if the contact already exists at your system and has an email - they will receive an email notification each time you respond with a public comment. Thus if you want to disable it:\n- Enter Zoho Desk Settings page\n- Customization > Notifications > Adding a public comment > false"
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
