    {
      "id": "027b4fb2-2f1b-4c2f-87c3-8b98d460a64a",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        688,
        -1616
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 4,
        "width": 960,
        "height": 624,
        "content": "# Telegram \u2194 Zoho Desk \u2014 Two-Way Support Integration\n\n## What does this workflow do?\n\nThis workflow connects a Telegram bot with Zoho Desk, allowing support teams to manage Telegram conversations directly from Zoho Desk.\n\nWhen a user sends a Telegram message, the workflow automatically identifies the user, creates a Zoho Desk contact if necessary, and adds the message to an existing open ticket or creates a new one.\n\nWhen a support agent adds a public comment in Zoho Desk, the reply is automatically delivered to the user's Telegram chat.\n\n## Key Features\n\n- **Two-way messaging:** Send user messages to Zoho Desk and agent replies back to Telegram.\n- **Automatic contact creation:** Create Zoho Desk contacts for new Telegram users.\n- **Ticket management:** Reuse an existing open ticket or create a new one.\n- **User mapping:** Store Telegram user IDs, chat IDs, and Zoho Desk contact IDs using n8n Data Tables.\n- **Message updates:** Process new and edited Telegram text messages.\n- **Webhook-based replies:** Receive Zoho Desk comment events without polling.\n\n## How It Works\n\n**Telegram \u2192 Zoho Desk:** Telegram message \u2192 Find or create contact \u2192 Find or create ticket \u2192 Add message as a private comment\n\n**Zoho Desk \u2192 Telegram:** Public agent comment \u2192 Zoho Desk webhook \u2192 Find Telegram chat \u2192 Send reply\n\n## Requirements\n\n- Telegram bot and Telegram API credentials\n- Zoho Desk account with API and webhook access\n- Zoho OAuth2 credentials\n\n**Before activating:** Complete the setup instructions, configure your credentials, and test both messaging directions."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
